<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24304" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆθεν </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆθε</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>El.</u>
			268
		</span></i>, cj. in <i><span class="en">
			Eup.
			7.1
		</span></i>
		<i><span class="en">
			D.
		</span></i>), Adv., a strengthd. form of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δή, ὡς Ζεὺς ἀνάσσοι δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					204
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς παῖδα δ. μὴ τέκοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					268
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ion</u>
				831
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί δὴ ἀνδρωθέντες δ. ποιήσουσι;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.138
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτι δ.</span>”
				<i>I suppose,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					297c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> more freq.
			ironically, <i>forsooth,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἵ μιν ἠθέλησαν ἀπολέσαι δ . . .</span>”
				<i>as he pretended,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.59
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. οὐδὲν ἱστορῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					382
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἐπὶ κωλύμῃ ἀλλὰ γνώμης
					παραινέσει δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.92
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				127
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.111
			</span></i>: freq. after <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς,</span> mostly
			with a word interposed, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέροντες ὡς ἄγρην δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.73
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς κατασκόπους δ. ἐόντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.136
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				6.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.5
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέντρον δ. ὡς ἔχων χερί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					949
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴσιμεν . . δ. ὡς θανούμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1119
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεατὴν δ., ὡς οὐκ ὄντ᾽ ἐμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ion</u>
					656
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>from that time, thenceforth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anacreont.
				1.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
